  "worked_solution": "The sum takes integer values of $i$ from $1$ to $4.$ So, we compute the terms for $i=1,2,3,4$ and write the sum, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(5-3i) & =\\overset{i\\,=\\,1}{\\overset{⏞}{(5-3(1))}}+\\overset{i\\,=\\,2}{\\overset{⏞}{(5-3(2))}}+\\overset{i\\,=\\,3}{\\overset{⏞}{(5-3(3))}}+\\overset{i\\,=\\,4}{\\overset{⏞}{(5-3(4))}} \\\\  & =(5-3)+(5-6)+(5-9)+(5-12) \\\\  & =2-1-4-7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
